{"id": "EUVD-2026-81924", "enisaUuid": "93bfe46b-1361-3b0a-9553-ee4a427a7655", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvirtio-net: Ensure that TCP packets don't overflow gso_segs\n\nThe user can specify any gso_size in a packet crafted with an AF_PACKET\nPACKET_VNET_HDR socket, even smaller than TCP_MIN_GSO_SIZE = 8. At the\nsame time, GSO_MAX_SIZE = 8 * GSO_MAX_SEGS = 8 * 65535. When the user\ncrafts a packet with gso_size < 8, there is a risk for partial GSO to\noverflow the 16-bit gso_segs field when dividing the SKB length by\ngso_size.\n\nAdjust gso_size of TCP packets to be at least TCP_MIN_GSO_SIZE = 8. Keep\ngso_size of UDP GSO packets, as gso_size=1 is valid and explicitly\ntested at tools/testing/selftests/net/tun.c:649.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:05:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3d111fe809773edbb4ae121e36253b7d683509a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f6667a081887c2b59c6f3dd86c1789ada563762", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/339f47ae04dcc6b5a730dd6bc70dddc8937c3260", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29bd12c7c5f9d6cf855b87bace18f71e9607f9e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e5ed3b98d1d8d251acfdccfeaa607453ad12954", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75c271c48f483af678e514734e10b2452410e08c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c27c449d455aafd9018a3cbab150f1c42c87923f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90063", "GHSA-86wj-v2pm-25hq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11895f3f-4be8-3849-becd-30856579b4ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7c6d2ecbda83150b2036a2b36b21381ad4667762 <c27c449d455aafd9018a3cbab150f1c42c87923f"}, {"id": "11e57272-aa23-33ce-afad-08de4d508714", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6.18 <5.7"}, {"id": "17ad5d77-cfde-3643-98f1-0eeba02344cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}},